.TH SQLICON 1 "" "sqlicon @sqli_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sqlicon \- interactive shell for Informix
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sqlicon
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Sqlicon
is a command-line interface for IBM Informix databases. It connects directly
using the Informix SQLI wire protocol (no Informix Client SDK required) and
provides an interactive SQL prompt, batch mode, and script execution.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-command \fIsql\fR
Execute a single SQL statement and exit.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-file \fIpath\fR
Execute SQL statements from a script file and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit. Must be used alone.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the shared libsqli/sqlicon version from CMake and exit. Must be used alone.
.TP
.B \-\-finderr \fIcode\fR
Look up a signed decimal Informix error code and exit. Must be used alone.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-profile \fIname\fR
Use a named connection profile (stored in ~/.config/sqlicon/profiles.conf).
.TP
.B \-\-profile\-create \fIname\fR
Create a connection profile from the given connection flags.
.TP
.B \-\-profile\-show \fIname\fR
Show profile connection details (password masked).
.TP
.B \-\-profile\-list
List all available connection profiles.
.TP
.B \-\-profile\-update \fIname\fR
Update a profile's fields from the given connection flags.
.TP
.B \-\-profile\-delete \fIname\fR
Delete a profile (requires \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-profile\-default \fIname\fR
Set the default profile name.
.TP
.B \-\-profile\-test \fIname\fR
Test the saved profile connection and exit. Connection environment overrides are not applied.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-secret
Show cleartext password in \fB\-\-profile\-show\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Confirm destructive actions (required for \fB\-\-profile\-delete\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-host \fIname\fR
Informix host name or IP address.
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIvalue\fR
Informix service name, numeric port (1..65535), or Unix socket path.
.TP
.B \-\-server \fIname\fR
Informix server name (from sqlhosts).
.TP
.B \-\-database \fIname\fR
Database name to connect to.
.TP
.B \-\-user \fIname\fR
User name for authentication.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIvalue\fR
Password for authentication (avoid in shell history).
.TP
.B \-\-client\-locale \fIvalue\fR
Client locale (e.g. en_US.utf8).
.TP
.B \-\-db\-locale \fIvalue\fR
Database locale (e.g. de_DE.CP1252).
.TP
.B \-\-connect-uri \fIuri\fR
Connect using an informix+onsoctcp, informix+onsocssl or informix+onipcstr URI.
The URI is self-contained: profiles and separate connection fields cannot be
combined with it. Include credentials and locales in the URI as needed.
Profile loading and CLI connection-environment merging are skipped for URIs.
.TP
.B \-\-log-level \fIlevel\fR
Set connection logging to none, error, warn, info or debug (default: error).
Logs go to stderr, or the file specified by SQLI_LOG_FILE.
.SH ARGUMENT RULES
Long value options accept both \fB--option value\fR and \fB--option=value\fR.
Use the latter for values beginning with a dash. Repeated options are errors.
An empty value is accepted only for passwords; \fB--password=\fR explicitly
sets an empty password and overrides both environment and profile values.
.PP
Command and file modes are mutually exclusive. Profile actions are mutually
exclusive and cannot be combined with SQL execution or --profile.
Connection fields are accepted for profile create/update, but not for other
profile actions. Profile update requires at least one field.
.PP
Profile create/update use explicit flags only. URI import is unsupported because
the profile format does not preserve URI transport settings.
.SH CONNECTION PRECEDENCE
For ordinary connections, explicit flags override environment values, which
override the named or default profile. Without --profile, the default profile
provides missing fields. For --profile-test, saved connection fields are used.
.SH MODES
If no mode option is provided, sqlicon determines the mode automatically:
.TP
.B Interactive mode
When stdin is a terminal (TTY), an interactive SQL prompt starts.
.TP
.B Batch mode
When stdin is redirected (e.g., piped from a file), SQL statements are
read from stdin until EOF.
.SH DOT COMMANDS
The following dot commands are available in interactive and batch modes:
.TP
.B .help
Show a list of dot commands.
.TP
.B .quit, .exit
Exit the shell.
.TP
.B .mode \fIMODE\fR
Set output mode: \fBaligned\fR (default), \fBcsv\fR, \fBline\fR, \fBjson\fR, \fBmarkdown\fR.
.TP
.B .width \fIIDX WIDTH\fR
Set minimum display width for column \fIIDX\fR in aligned mode.
.TP
.B .width off
Reset all width overrides.
.TP
.B .headers on|off
Toggle column headers in output.
.TP
.B .bail on|off
Stop (\fBon\fR) or continue (\fBoff\fR) on SQL errors.
.TP
.B .timer on|off
Show statement execution time on stderr.
.TP
.B .nullvalue \fITEXT\fR
Set the display text for NULL values (default: "NULL").
.TP
.B .output \fIFILE|stdout\fR
Redirect output to a file persistently, or to stdout.
.TP
.B .once \fIFILE\fR
Redirect the next statement's output to a file, then resume normal output.
.TP
.B .read \fIFILE\fR
Execute SQL and dot commands from a script file.
.TP
.B .explain on|off
Execute SET EXPLAIN ON/OFF to show query execution plans.
.TP
.B .use \fIDATABASE\fR
Switch the active database in the current session.
.TP
.B .databases
List available databases.
.TP
.B .status
Show current session and database metadata.
.TP
.B .schema \fITABLE\fR
Show table columns and raw Informix data types.
.TP
.B .indexes \fITABLE\fR
Show index metadata for a table.
.TP
.B .constraints \fITABLE\fR
Show table constraints (PRIMARY KEY, FOREIGN KEY, UNIQUE, CHECK).
.TP
.B .dump [\fITABLE\fR]
Export table rows as SQL INSERT statements. Omit TABLE to dump all user tables.
.TP
.B .import \fIFILE TABLE\fR
Import a CSV file (with header row) into the specified table.
.TP
.B .tables
List user tables in the current database.
.SH PROFILES
Connection profiles are stored in \fI~/.config/sqlicon/profiles.conf\fR.
Passwords are encrypted using AES-256-GCM with a key derived from the
user's UID and hostname. Profiles protect against accidental file
disclosure but not against an attacker with access to the same
machine and account.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Connection defaults: SQLI_HOST, SQLI_PORT, SQLI_SERVER, SQLI_DATABASE
(fallback SQLI_DB), SQLI_USER, SQLI_PASSWORD, SQLI_CLIENT_LOCALE,
SQLI_DB_LOCALE and SQLI_LOG_LEVEL.
.PP
INFORMIXSERVER, CLIENT_LOCALE and DB_LOCALE are fallbacks for their respective
SQLI_ variables. Empty environment values are treated as unset, except
SQLI_PASSWORD, where an empty string represents an empty password.
.PP
The profile file is \fI~/.config/sqlicon/profiles.conf\fR on POSIX systems
and \fI%APPDATA%\\sqlicon\\profiles.conf\fR on Windows.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Connect interactively using a profile:
.B sqlicon \-p mydb
.TP
Execute a single query:
.B sqlicon \-p mydb \-c "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM orders"
.TP
Run a script file:
.B sqlicon \-p mydb \-f migrate.sql
.TP
Pipe SQL from stdin:
.B echo "SELECT * FROM systables" | sqlicon \-p mydb
.TP
Export query results as JSON:
.B echo \e".mode json\\\\nSELECT * FROM products" | sqlicon \-p mydb
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/sqlicon/libsqli/issues
.SH AUTHOR
the sqlicon authors <sqlicon0x7bc@gmail.com>
